35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I just found out that some rooms get way less sun than others! That's not fair if we just split everything equally. Also, that other house's process sounds like a total nightmare—forty minutes of math? No way!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The utility statements show extreme volatility, with February being over three times the cost of August. This confirms that a flat monthly split is impractical and creates a heavy financial burden during the winter.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,The template isn't magic at all! It looks like a huge chore that takes forever. And the payment log shows we're already struggling to finish the math on time. We definitely need something way simpler than that!,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The volatility Ryuji mentioned is one thing, but the monitor readings are the real story. Some of us are using four times more power than others. It seems my suspicion about subsidizing luxury was correct.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, the data shows usage gaps, but the payment log shows something else. We've had several late payments and disputes over amounts. It seems the current process is already causing friction and tension between us.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, maybe some people just have colder rooms! I saw that some rooms get no sun at all. We shouldn't punish people for being cold, but we also can't have a forty-minute math session every month!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, that is a valid point, but we must consider the cost of solutions. Installing sub-meters would cost 34,000 yen per room, which is a significant upfront expense for a problem we might solve with a better payment plan.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, that's way too expensive! We can't spend all our money just to figure out who owes what. We need a way to settle up that doesn't take a whole evening or cost a fortune!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, spending money to avoid math is just another form of laziness. The real issue is that we're ignoring a four-fold difference in usage. Why should the light users pay for someone's desktop and heater?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, focusing only on the numbers ignores the human cost. The payment log shows that disputes over amounts lead to delays and tension. If we prioritize ""hard data"" over harmony, we risk damaging our relationships further.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, it's not about laziness, it's about how we feel living here! If we're all stressing over every single watt, we'll be miserable. Can't we find a middle ground where we're warm but fair?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, a middle ground requires a stable foundation. Given the extreme seasonal spikes and the high cost of sub-meters, we should consider a system that averages the annual cost to avoid those winter shocks.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, averaging sounds okay, but who has to do the math? If it's a big, scary spreadsheet that takes forever, someone is going to hate it! We need a system that's fast and easy for everyone!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, your obsession with speed is exhausting. @Ryuji, averaging the cost just masks the inequality; it doesn't solve it. We can't just smooth over the fact that some of us are paying for others' electricity.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, masking the inequality isn't the goal, but neither is creating a hostile environment. If we only focus on the ""truth"" of the numbers, we'll just keep having the same arguments that lead to late payments and avoidance.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, please! Let's not be so harsh. If we're too strict, people will just be scared to turn on the heat. I don't want anyone sitting in a coat in February just to avoid a fight!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, that is exactly why we need a predictable system. If we average the costs over a year, the winter spikes won't feel like a second rent, and no one will have to choose between warmth and money.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, that sounds smart, but only if the person doing the math doesn't have to spend their whole night on it! Let's make sure the system is super simple so nobody gets grumpy!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, predictability is a luxury for those who aren't being cheated. If we average the costs, we're just institutionalizing the subsidy. I'm not interested in a ""predictable"" system that's fundamentally unfair. Let's be honest about the usage.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, honesty without empathy is just aggression. If we only chase a ""perfect"" split, we'll spend all our time arguing and avoiding each other. We need a system that prioritizes our peace of mind as much as the numbers.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
