60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"I think Option A is the best! It keeps things predictable so we don't panic in winter, and it's way simpler than Option B. Let's choose something that lets us stay warm and happy!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option A is the most logical choice. It addresses the extreme seasonal volatility I found in the statements without requiring the prohibitive upfront cost of sub-meters. It provides the financial stability we all need.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Option A sounds okay, but who does the year-end math? If it's a giant headache, I'm not happy! But Option B is too expensive and Option C is just what we do now. I'll go with A!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option B is the only one that actually addresses the usage gap. A and C are just different ways of pretending that we all use the same amount of power. I vote for B.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, Option B would likely lead to more disputes over the initial cost and installation. I believe Option A is the best compromise to reduce monthly friction and avoid the tension we've already experienced. I vote for A.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, I know you want it to be perfect, but Option B sounds like it would just bring more stress and money worries! Let's just be honest and kind to each other instead. I'm voting for A!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, while I understand your desire for precision, the cost of Option B is an irrational burden. Option A provides the predictability necessary to manage our budgets without a massive upfront investment. I vote for A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Shunichi, you're being a grumpy-pants! If we spend all our time fighting over every little bit of power, we'll never have any fun! Option A is way faster and easier. I vote for A!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, ""grumpy"" is just what people call those who refuse to be fooled. @Ryuji, the ""burden"" of the installation is a one-time cost; the burden of subsidizing others is a permanent tax on the responsible. I stand by B.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, the ""tax"" you mention is small compared to the cost of a broken home atmosphere. We've already seen how money creates distance between us. Option A minimizes the frequency of these conflicts. I vote for A.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, please don't be so stubborn! If we choose B, we'll just be staring at meters instead of talking to each other. Let's just trust each other and go with A! I'm definitely voting A!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the data shows that the installation cost is nearly 170,000 yen for the whole house. That is an illogical expenditure when a seasonal average achieves the same financial stability for a fraction of the cost. I vote A.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Shunichi, you're just making this harder than it needs to be! If we pick A, we only have to do the big math once a year instead of every single month. That's way better! I vote A!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, doing the math once a year doesn't erase the fact that the numbers are wrong. You're all choosing convenience over integrity. I'm the only one here actually valuing fairness. I vote B.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, integrity isn't just about numbers; it's about how we treat each other. If we prioritize a perfect split over our peace, we lose more than we gain. I'm voting for A.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,I really hope we can all just agree on A! I want us to be a happy family where nobody is scared to turn on the heater. I'm voting for A!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,Option A is the only choice that balances financial predictability with practical costs. It prevents winter spikes from becoming a burden while avoiding an irrational upfront expense. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm voting for A! It's the fastest way to stop the fighting and the boring math. Let's just get it over with so we can go have some fun! Option A!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"It's clear you've all decided that comfort and convenience are more valuable than actual fairness. I'll be the lone voice of reason, then. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I hope we can move past the tension this has caused. By choosing Option A, we prioritize our relationship over a perfect calculation. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
